@@ -4,12 +4,18 @@ A small team notes app. Next.js App Router + TypeScript + Tailwind.
 
 ## Status
 
-- Users live in `src/lib/users.ts` as an in-memory list.
-- `/dashboard` shows the current user and the team.
-- There is no sign-in, no billing, and no email yet.
+- Auth is real: email/password and Google sign-in via [Better Auth](https://www.better-auth.com), stored in a local SQLite file (`notely.db`, gitignored).
+- `src/lib/users.ts` is now backed by that database instead of a hardcoded array — see `src/lib/auth.ts`.
+- `/dashboard` requires a signed-in session (`src/app/dashboard/layout.tsx`); signed-out visitors are redirected to `/sign-in`.
+- There is no billing or email yet.
 
 ## Develop
 
 ```bash
+cp .env.example .env.local   # fill in BETTER_AUTH_SECRET at least; Google is optional
+npm install
+npx auth migrate -y          # creates notely.db with the user/session/account/verification tables
 npm run dev
 ```
+
+Google sign-in is disabled automatically until `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` / `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` in `.env.local` are set to real values from the [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials) (authorized redirect URI: `{BETTER_AUTH_URL}/api/auth/callback/google`). Email/password sign-in works with just `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` set.
